  "messages": [
    "Good morning, Coldwater. Everything you see today was in somebody's flat last week.",
    "They couldn't pay. You can.",
    "Lot one. A two-slice toaster. Barely burnt.",
    "Look at that chrome, Jolene.",
    "There's a crumb tray, Vance. It comes out.",
    "They don't make them like that any more. They don't make them at all, actually. The factory's a car park.",
    "Vance, I've got a caller on line three.",
    "Put her through, Pim.",
    "She says that's her toaster.",
    "Was. Was her toaster.",
    "She wants to buy it back.",
    "Then the price just went up. Sentimental value.",
    "Forty credits.",
    "She's crying.",
    "Forty-five.",
    "Lot two. A family photograph, frame included.",
    "Lovely frame. Real wood. You can take the family out.",
    "Vance, that's my sister.",
    "So it is. Small world.",
    "She said she was moving.",
    "She did move. Twelve credits, Coldwater.",
    "Line one wants the toaster and the sister.",
    "The sister isn't for sale. Yet.",
    "Vance, there's a man on line six. He's from the bank.",
    "Tell him we're live.",
    "He says he knows. He says he's in reception.",
    "He wants the counter, Vance.",
    "And the phones.",
    "You heard him, Coldwater. Everything must go."
  ],
